<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tian Heng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/202-bce">202 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian">Tian</a> Heng (died 202 BCE) was a member of the royal house of the old state of Qi who, after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>, made himself and his relatives kings of Qi and fought both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-xin">Han Xin</a> conquered Qi he fled to an island with some 500 followers. Summoned by Liu Bang, now emperor, he killed himself rather than submit, and his followers did the same.</p></div>
